.TH dls 1 "Build date: @DLS_COMPILE_DATE@" "version @PROJECT_VERSION@" "Dynamic Legged Systems Framework"

.\" ============================================================================
.SH dls
.\" ============================================================================

Dynamic Legged Systems software framework for the HyQ robot family.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" ============================================================================

.B dls
[ --version | -v ]
[ --help | -h ]
[ --docs | -d ]
[ --robot=robotname | -rrobotname ]
[ --layers=layers | -llayers ]
[ [ --simulation | -s ] | [ --hardware | -H ] ]
[ --core | -c ]


.\" ============================================================================
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" ============================================================================

.PP
This program launches the control framework for the HyQ robot family.

.PP
The framework is divided into separate layers. These layers may be launched
inside the same process space, inside different processes or on different
machines in any configuration.

Command autocompletion is available for both the bash and the zsh shells.
.PP
The layers available are:
.RS
Control Layer
.\" ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.RS
Handles launching of controllers and gait generators. Takes care of
communication with the hardware or simulation. Takes corrective action if a gait
generator or controller crashes
.RE

Console Layer
.\" ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.RS
Provides a command-line interface into the framework. The console supports tab
completion. The console provides a 'help' command that may be used to learn more
about unknown commands.

.PP
Note that commands are added to and removed from the console dynamically as
components are added to and removed from the framework. Since commands may be
added by 3rd-party plugins, each command is assigned a namespace. If a
registered command has a unique name, it may be entered directly into the
console. However, if multiple commands of the same name exist, the console will
list the namespaces in which the command is found. In such cases, it is
necessary to call the command using the form 'namespace_name::command'.
.RE

Estimation Layer
.\" ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.RS
This layer is responsible for launching and managing state estimators.
.RE

Hardware Layer
.\" ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.RS
This layer is responsible for communication between the framework and the robot
hardware or simulation. In simulation mode this layer may be launched anywhere.
When running on the robot, however, it must be launched on the actual robot
hardware.
.RE

Log Layer
.\" ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.RS
This layer is responsible for redirecting all the log information to files or
standard output for recording a session. The log output is in a format that can
easily be filtered with standard Unix tools.

Log information may be inspected in realtime by launching a log layer that
prints everything to standard out, and then filtering with tools such as 'grep'
or 'awk'.
.RE

.RE
.\" ============================================================================
.SH OPTIONS
.\" ============================================================================
.TP
.B --help, -h
Prints a help message and exits.

.TP
.B --version, -v
Prints the version and exits.

.TP
.B --docs, -d
Opens development documentation in a browser.

.TP
.BI "--robot=" "robotname" ", " " " "-r" "robotname"
Specifies the robot that the framework is running on. Necessary when specifying
the control, estimation or hardware layers. 'robotname' may be one of 'hyq'
or 'hyqreal'.

.TP
.B --simulation, -s
Runs the framework in simulation mode (This is the default mode).

.TP
.B --core, -c
Launches the framework in core mode. This mode launches an instance of roscore
in case some controllers need to use ros. An instance of the framework launched
in this mode may create and manage new layers by issuing the appropriate
commands from a console instance.

.TP
.B --hardware, -H
Runs the framework for the real hardware (as opposed to in simulation).

.TP
.BI "--layers=" "layernames" ", " " " "-l" "layernames"
Launches the layers specified by the coma-separated list 'layernames'. Available
options are 'console', 'control', 'estimation', 'hardware' and 'log'.

If the layers are not specified, the framework will default to "estimation",
"control" and "console"


